<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <changeSet id="20260817000001-01" author="Ivica Cardic">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="project" columnName="visibility"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>

        <addColumn tableName="project">
            <column name="visibility" type="INT" defaultValueNumeric="1">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>
        <comment>
            Projects default to WORKSPACE (1) — shared with the owning workspace, which is the pre-visibility behaviour
            for every existing row. PRIVATE (0) is opt-in via setProjectVisibility (EE). Ordinal of ResourceVisibility.
        </comment>
        <!--
            Deliberately an EMPTY rollback, not a dropColumn, and not an omitted block.

            The precondition above means this changeset cannot know whether it created the column. When it fires
            (visibility already present, added by hand or by a restored dump) the changeset is MARK_RAN without doing
            anything, and a rollback that drops the column would then destroy every project's visibility setting,
            data this changeset never wrote. Omitting the block does not avoid that: Liquibase auto-generates the
            inverse of addColumn, so the drop would still happen, just invisibly.

            The cost of the empty block is an inert leftover column after a rollback. It is NOT NULL with a default of
            1, so pre-visibility code that never names it still inserts fine, and re-applying this changeset is a no-op
            through the same precondition. Recoverable either way, where the drop is not.
        -->
        <rollback/>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
